---
import Shell from '../../layouts/Shell.astro';
import LegalNav from '../../components/LegalNav.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Shell
	title='Disclaimers — ArenaSwap'
	description='ArenaSwap is not affiliated with ESPN or any league, comes with no warranty, and depends on scores it does not control.'
	path='legal/terms/'
>
	<div class='container'>
		<div class='page-head'>
			<h1 class='page-title'>Disclaimers.</h1>
			<p class='page-lede'>
				ArenaSwap is a free extension written by sports fans. Here is what that does and does not
				entitle you to.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class='reading-shell'>
			<LegalNav current='legal/terms/' />

			<div class='prose'>
				<h2>No affiliation</h2>
				<p>
					ArenaSwap is not affiliated with, sponsored by, endorsed by or connected to ESPN, the NFL,
					NBA, WNBA, NHL, MLB, MLS, NWSL, NCAA, UFL, FIFA, UEFA, the International Olympic
					Committee, or any other league, club, broadcaster or streaming service. League and team
					names, marks and crests belong to their owners and are used here only to identify games.
				</p>

				<h2>It is not a streaming service</h2>
				<p>
					ArenaSwap does not host, rebroadcast, decrypt, unlock or provide access to any game. It
					switches between browser tabs you opened yourself, on services you are entitled to watch.
					Whether you can watch a given game is a matter between you and whoever sells it.
				</p>

				<h2>Data comes from somewhere else</h2>
				<p>
					Scores, clocks, schedules, odds and win probabilities all come from ESPN. ArenaSwap does
					not control that data, cannot guarantee it is accurate, complete, current or available,
					and has no say in when it changes. Data may be delayed, wrong or missing, and a
					stream usually runs behind the data feed. Do not treat anything in this extension as an
					official score, and do not bet on one.
				</p>

				<h2>PowerScore is an opinion</h2>
				<p>
					PowerScore estimates how exciting a game looks right now from public numbers. It is not a
					prediction, a probability, a betting model or a statement of fact, and it will sometimes
					send you away from the game you wanted to watch. That is
					what <a href={`${base}faq/`}>sensitivity, cooldown and favorite teams</a> are for.
				</p>

				<h2>No warranty</h2>
				<p>
					The software is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied,
					including merchantability and fitness for a particular purpose. Nobody involved in
					ArenaSwap is liable for any damages arising from its use, including a missed game-winner.
					The full text is on the <a href={`${base}legal/licenses/`}>licenses page</a>.
				</p>

				<h2>Availability</h2>
				<p>
					ArenaSwap is free, unfunded and maintained in spare time. Browsers change the rules for
					extensions, the services it reads from change without warning, and nothing here comes
					with a service level agreement. A feature may change or go away in a version. When one does,
					the <a href={`${base}releases/`}>release notes</a> say so.
				</p>

				<h2>Nothing here is legal advice</h2>
				<p>
					These pages describe how a browser extension behaves. They are not advice, and they
					create no contract beyond the ISC License the software ships under.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</Shell>
